wers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think the current `clamp_to_embedder` is correct. Currently you can have an embedded window where you can drag it outside of its embedding window, but resizing the parent window moves it back into view, which is a strange behavior. It was intended that \"windows that are clamped to their embedder are now automatically shifted/resized on popup, and when the parent is resized.\" (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/75141#issuecomment-1483656600), but in `Viewport::_set_size` it never checked if the child had `clamp_to_embedder`. \r\n\r\nSo I don't think `clamp_to_embedder` is intended to have a different purpose, and the properties should be merged into one.\r\n\r\n- Also see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99946","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119247#pullrequestreview-4430015512","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119247","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119247#pullrequestreview-4430015512"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119247"}},"submitted_at":"2026-06-04T17:34:56Z","commit_id":"4d4a92f56b82c74bcd297bfc20832d9e172039db"}]